--format.estate.lead.base--:
For each lead, use this exact fenced block with a JSON object payload: ```neup.estate.lead.base
{"id":"leadId","name":"leadName","email":"leadEmail","phone":"leadPhone"}
```. Omit optional keys when their values are unavailable; always include id and name. Do not add text inside the object outside its fields.

--format.estate.property.saved--:
For each saved property, use one fenced block with this exact name and a JSON object payload: ```neup.estate.property.saved
{"propertyId":"propertyId","title":"propertyTitle","price":"price","location":"location","type":"propertyType","image":"imageUrl"}
```. Include only fields present in the property data; propertyId or id and at least one of title or name are required. Do not output property records as plain text or unfenced objects.
